Version 2.0
=================

First public release.

mplib provides electrostatic potentials (unary self-energy and pairwise
interaction, each with a faster polynomial-approximation variant) for ions
confined in slit (2D) and cylindrical (1D) metallic nanopores, via a C
library with Python (ctypes) bindings. See README for the full function
list, references, and build instructions.

- Fortran is optional: only needed for the Towhee-callable wrapper test
  (tests/fortran/); the C library and Python bindings don't require it.
- Real test suite: tests/python/test_mplib.py (pytest, the primary suite)
  plus tests/c/test-slit.c and test-cylinder.c, both wired into
  `make check`.
- Illustrative usage scripts live in examples/ (not part of the automated
  build/tests).
